IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wica-types`
IMPORT `wica-insurance-offences`
IMPORT `wica-administration`

-- Work Injury Compensation Act 2019 — TESTS FOR GOALS 7 AND 8: insurance and
-- offences, and the small rules among the administrative provisions.
--
-- Expected values are worked from ../source/WICA2019.txt: ss 24-34, 34O-34P,
-- 35(8)-(9), 40, 47-47G, 50(4), 60-62, 68(6)-(7), 70, 72-73, 76-77, 82(3).

§ `Tests — Goals 7 and 8`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN insured IS A BOOLEAN, excluded IS A BOOLEAN, mlc IS A BOOLEAN, steps IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Insurance position`
`insurance` insured excluded mlc steps MEANS
    `Insurance position` WITH
        `insured under approved policies with designated insurers for every worker` IS insured
        `in an excluded class prescribed under s 24(2)(a)`           IS excluded
        `a seafarer covered by Maritime Labour Convention security`  IS mlc
        `took all reasonable steps to ascertain the matters in s 25(3)` IS steps

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, wu IS A BOOLEAN, rec IS A BOOLEAN, deb IS A BOOLEAN, recon IS A BOOLEAN, void IS A BOOLEAN, told IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Insolvency facts`
`insolvency` a wu rec deb recon void told MEANS
    `Insolvency facts` WITH
        `bankrupt, or a composition or scheme with creditors`       IS a
        `winding-up proceedings commenced`                          IS wu
        `a receiver or manager appointed`                           IS rec
        `debenture holders took possession under a floating charge` IS deb
        `only a voluntary winding up for reconstruction or amalgamation` IS recon
        `the contract is void or voidable other than for premiums`  IS void
        `the employee gave the insurer notice as soon as practicable` IS told

GIVEN o IS AN Offence
GIVETH AN `Earlier conviction`
`a conviction for` o MEANS
    `Earlier conviction` WITH `offence` IS o, `under the repealed Act` IS FALSE, `repealed Act provision` IS "", `under the old regulation 3(5)` IS FALSE

-- the offence field is not read for a repealed-Act conviction; any value will do
GIVEN p IS A STRING
GIVETH AN `Earlier conviction`
`a conviction under the repealed Act, s` p MEANS
    `Earlier conviction` WITH `offence` IS `s 82(3) — contravening the regulations`, `under the repealed Act` IS TRUE, `repealed Act provision` IS p, `under the old regulation 3(5)` IS FALSE

`a conviction under the old regulation 3(5)` MEANS
    `Earlier conviction` WITH `offence` IS `s 82(3) — contravening the regulations`, `under the repealed Act` IS FALSE, `repealed Act provision` IS "", `under the old regulation 3(5)` IS TRUE

GIVEN o IS AN Offence, r IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`fine for` o r MEANS (`the maximum penalty for` o `, a repeat offender:` r)'s `fine`

GIVEN o IS AN Offence, r IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`months for` o r MEANS (`the maximum penalty for` o `, a repeat offender:` r)'s `imprisonment in months`

GIVEN pos IS A BOOLEAN, a IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Officer facts`
`officer` pos a b c MEANS
    `Officer facts` WITH
        `an officer, partner, or manager able to influence the conduct` IS pos
        `consented, connived or conspired`                               IS a
        `knowingly concerned in or party to it`                          IS b
        `knew or ought to have known, and did not take all reasonable steps` IS c

§§ `Goal 7a — the duty to insure (ss 24, 25, 34O, 34P, 67(4))`

--                                          insured excluded MLC   steps
#ASSERT     `the insurance duty is met:` (`insurance` TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT     `the insurance duty is met:` (`insurance` FALSE TRUE  FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT     `the insurance duty is met:` (`insurance` FALSE FALSE TRUE  FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the insurance duty is met:` (`insurance` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 25(3): not knowing is no defence unless all reasonable steps were taken
#ASSERT     `the s 25(1) / 34P(1) offence is made out on` (`insurance` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `, ignorance pleaded:` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the s 25(1) / 34P(1) offence is made out on` (`insurance` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)  `, ignorance pleaded:` TRUE
#ASSERT     `the s 25(1) / 34P(1) offence is made out on` (`insurance` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)  `, ignorance pleaded:` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the s 25(1) / 34P(1) offence is made out on` (`insurance` TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE) `, ignorance pleaded:` FALSE

§§ `Goal 7b — the policy (ss 26, 27)`

#ASSERT     `an approved policy, compulsory terms:` TRUE `, derogating term:` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `an approved policy, compulsory terms:` TRUE `, derogating term:` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `an approved policy, compulsory terms:` FALSE `, derogating term:` FALSE
-- s 26(3)-(4): as if compliant, but not beyond the prescribed minimum
#ASSERT `what the insurer of a purported policy must pay, of compensation` 500000 `, the minimum` (JUST 300000) EQUALS 300000
#ASSERT `what the insurer of a purported policy must pay, of compensation` 200000 `, the minimum` (JUST 300000) EQUALS 200000
#ASSERT `what the insurer of a purported policy must pay, of compensation` 500000 `, the minimum` NOTHING EQUALS 500000
-- s 27(1)
#ASSERT NOT `the insurer may raise the defence, it being double insurance:` TRUE

§§ `Goal 7c — insolvency (ss 28, 29)`

--                                                                           bankrupt w-up  recv  deb   recon void  told
#ASSERT     `the employer's rights against the insurer pass to the worker:` (`insolvency` TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT     `the employer's rights against the insurer pass to the worker:` (`insolvency` FALSE TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT     `the employer's rights against the insurer pass to the worker:` (`insolvency` FALSE FALSE TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT     `the employer's rights against the insurer pass to the worker:` (`insolvency` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the employer's rights against the insurer pass to the worker:` (`insolvency` FALSE TRUE  FALSE FALSE TRUE  FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the employer's rights against the insurer pass to the worker:` (`insolvency` TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE  FALSE)
#ASSERT     `the employer's rights against the insurer pass to the worker:` (`insolvency` TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE  TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the employer's rights against the insurer pass to the worker:` (`insolvency` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 28(2)(b), (3)
#ASSERT `the balance the worker may prove for, liability` 100000 `, insurer's liability` 60000 EQUALS 40000
#ASSERT `the balance the worker may prove for, liability` 50000 `, insurer's liability` 60000 EQUALS 0

§§ `Goal 7d, 7e — providers and designated insurers (ss 30, 31, 34)`

#ASSERT     `providing it is an offence under s 30, provider` `anyone else` `, approved:` TRUE `, within the Act:` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `providing it is an offence under s 30, provider` `a designated insurer of the right kind, not suspended` `, approved:` TRUE `, within the Act:` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `providing it is an offence under s 30, provider` `an insurance intermediary for such an insurer` `, approved:` TRUE `, within the Act:` TRUE
#ASSERT     `providing it is an offence under s 30, provider` `a designated insurer of the right kind, not suspended` `, approved:` FALSE `, within the Act:` TRUE
-- s 30(5): health or accident cover, or excess-only cover, is not within s 30
#ASSERT NOT `providing it is an offence under s 30, provider` `anyone else` `, approved:` FALSE `, within the Act:` FALSE
-- s 34(1)(b): $30,000 per failure
#ASSERT `the most the Commissioner may impose on a designated insurer, failures being` 3 EQUALS 90000
-- s 31(6)
#ASSERT     `the designation, until` (JUST (YMD 2027 12 31)) `, cancelled` NOTHING `, is in force on` (YMD 2027 12 31)
#ASSERT NOT `the designation, until` (JUST (YMD 2027 12 31)) `, cancelled` NOTHING `, is in force on` (YMD 2028 1 1)
#ASSERT     `the designation, until` NOTHING `, cancelled` (JUST (YMD 2026 6 1)) `, is in force on` (YMD 2026 5 31)
#ASSERT NOT `the designation, until` NOTHING `, cancelled` (JUST (YMD 2026 6 1)) `, is in force on` (YMD 2026 6 1)

§§ `Goal 8a — repeat offenders`

-- s 25(2): (a) s 25(1), (b) s 34P(1), (c) repealed Act s 35(1)(b)
#ASSERT     `a repeat offender for` `s 25(1) — employer not insured` `, with earlier convictions` (LIST `a conviction for` `s 25(1) — employer not insured`)
#ASSERT     `a repeat offender for` `s 25(1) — employer not insured` `, with earlier convictions` (LIST `a conviction for` `s 34P(1) — platform operator not insured`)
#ASSERT     `a repeat offender for` `s 25(1) — employer not insured` `, with earlier convictions` (LIST `a conviction under the repealed Act, s` "35(1)(b)")
#ASSERT NOT `a repeat offender for` `s 25(1) — employer not insured` `, with earlier convictions` (LIST `a conviction under the repealed Act, s` "35(1)(a)")
#ASSERT NOT `a repeat offender for` `s 25(1) — employer not insured` `, with earlier convictions` (LIST `a conviction for` `s 25(4) — employer deducting insurance cost from earnings`)
#ASSERT NOT `a repeat offender for` `s 25(1) — employer not insured` `, with earlier convictions` EMPTY
-- s 34P(5): (i) s 34P(4), (ii) s 25(4), (iii) repealed s 35(1)(a)
#ASSERT     `a repeat offender for` `s 34P(4) — platform operator deducting insurance cost from earnings` `, with earlier convictions` (LIST `a conviction for` `s 25(4) — employer deducting insurance cost from earnings`)
#ASSERT     `a repeat offender for` `s 34P(4) — platform operator deducting insurance cost from earnings` `, with earlier convictions` (LIST `a conviction under the repealed Act, s` "35(1)(a)")
-- s 30(2C): s 30(1) or (2A), either way; s 30(3A): only s 30(3)
#ASSERT     `a repeat offender for` `s 30(2A) — unauthorised provider of platform operator insurance` `, with earlier convictions` (LIST `a conviction for` `s 30(1) — unauthorised provider of employer insurance`)
#ASSERT NOT `a repeat offender for` `s 30(3) — insurance that is not an approved policy` `, with earlier convictions` (LIST `a conviction for` `s 30(1) — unauthorised provider of employer insurance`)
#ASSERT     `a repeat offender for` `s 30(3) — insurance that is not an approved policy` `, with earlier convictions` (LIST `a conviction for` `s 30(3) — insurance that is not an approved policy`)
-- s 35(9): s 35(8), or regulation 3(5) of the old Regulations
#ASSERT     `a repeat offender for` `s 35(8) — failing to give the Commissioner notice of an accident` `, with earlier convictions` (LIST `a conviction under the old regulation 3(5)`)
#ASSERT NOT `a repeat offender for` `s 61(1) — failing to pay compensation` `, with earlier convictions` (LIST `a conviction under the old regulation 3(5)`)
-- s 61(2), (4): repealed s 35(2)(a), (b)
#ASSERT     `a repeat offender for` `s 61(1) — failing to pay compensation` `, with earlier convictions` (LIST `a conviction under the repealed Act, s` "35(2)(a)")
#ASSERT NOT `a repeat offender for` `s 61(1) — failing to pay compensation` `, with earlier convictions` (LIST `a conviction under the repealed Act, s` "35(2)(b)")
#ASSERT     `a repeat offender for` `s 61(3) — failing to deposit interest` `, with earlier convictions` (LIST `a conviction under the repealed Act, s` "35(2)(b)")
-- s 61(5) and s 50(4): "a second or subsequent conviction"
#ASSERT     `a repeat offender for` `s 61(5) — failing to make a directed deposit` `, with earlier convictions` (LIST `a conviction for` `s 61(5) — failing to make a directed deposit`)
#ASSERT     `a repeat offender for` `s 50(4) — failing to comply with a direction` `, with earlier convictions` (LIST `a conviction for` `s 50(4) — failing to comply with a direction`)
-- s 62(2): repealed s 35(2)(c)
#ASSERT     `a repeat offender for` `s 62(1) — false or misleading information` `, with earlier convictions` (LIST `a conviction under the repealed Act, s` "35(2)(c)")
-- s 62(4): (a) for s 62(3)(a), s 62(3)(a) or (b), or repealed s 35(2)(f); (b) for s 62(3)(b), only s 62(3)(a) or (b)
#ASSERT     `a repeat offender for` `s 62(3)(a) — dishonestly obtaining compensation` `, with earlier convictions` (LIST `a conviction under the repealed Act, s` "35(2)(f)")
#ASSERT NOT `a repeat offender for` `s 62(3)(b) — dishonestly avoiding liability to pay compensation` `, with earlier convictions` (LIST `a conviction under the repealed Act, s` "35(2)(f)")
#ASSERT     `a repeat offender for` `s 62(3)(b) — dishonestly avoiding liability to pay compensation` `, with earlier convictions` (LIST `a conviction for` `s 62(3)(a) — dishonestly obtaining compensation`)
-- s 68(7): repealed s 35(2)(e)
#ASSERT     `a repeat offender for` `s 68(6) — obstructing the Commissioner or an investigation officer` `, with earlier convictions` (LIST `a conviction under the repealed Act, s` "35(2)(e)")
-- s 82(3): no repeat tier
#ASSERT NOT `a repeat offender for` `s 82(3) — contravening the regulations` `, with earlier convictions` (LIST `a conviction for` `s 82(3) — contravening the regulations`)

§§ `Goal 8b — maximum penalties`

#ASSERT `fine for` `s 25(1) — employer not insured` FALSE EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `months for` `s 25(1) — employer not insured` FALSE EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `fine for` `s 25(1) — employer not insured` TRUE EQUALS 20000
#ASSERT `months for` `s 25(1) — employer not insured` TRUE EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `fine for` `s 25(4) — employer deducting insurance cost from earnings` FALSE EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `months for` `s 25(4) — employer deducting insurance cost from earnings` TRUE EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `fine for` `s 34P(1) — platform operator not insured` TRUE EQUALS 20000
#ASSERT `fine for` `s 34P(4) — platform operator deducting insurance cost from earnings` TRUE EQUALS 10000
-- s 30: per insurance policy, no imprisonment
#ASSERT `fine for` `s 30(1) — unauthorised provider of employer insurance` FALSE EQUALS 80000
#ASSERT `fine for` `s 30(2A) — unauthorised provider of platform operator insurance` TRUE EQUALS 160000
#ASSERT `fine for` `s 30(3) — insurance that is not an approved policy` TRUE EQUALS 160000
#ASSERT `months for` `s 30(3) — insurance that is not an approved policy` TRUE EQUALS 0
-- s 35(8): a fine only, the first time; imprisonment only for a repeat
#ASSERT `fine for` `s 35(8) — failing to give the Commissioner notice of an accident` FALSE EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `months for` `s 35(8) — failing to give the Commissioner notice of an accident` FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `fine for` `s 35(8) — failing to give the Commissioner notice of an accident` TRUE EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `months for` `s 35(8) — failing to give the Commissioner notice of an accident` TRUE EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `fine for` `s 50(4) — failing to comply with a direction` TRUE EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `months for` `s 50(4) — failing to comply with a direction` FALSE EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `fine for` `s 61(1) — failing to pay compensation` FALSE EQUALS 15000
#ASSERT `fine for` `s 61(3) — failing to deposit interest` TRUE EQUALS 30000
#ASSERT `fine for` `s 61(5) — failing to make a directed deposit` TRUE EQUALS 30000
#ASSERT `months for` `s 61(5) — failing to make a directed deposit` FALSE EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `fine for` `s 62(1) — false or misleading information` FALSE EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `fine for` `s 62(3)(a) — dishonestly obtaining compensation` FALSE EQUALS 15000
#ASSERT `fine for` `s 62(3)(b) — dishonestly avoiding liability to pay compensation` TRUE EQUALS 30000
#ASSERT `months for` `s 62(3)(b) — dishonestly avoiding liability to pay compensation` TRUE EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `fine for` `s 68(6) — obstructing the Commissioner or an investigation officer` TRUE EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `months for` `s 68(6) — obstructing the Commissioner or an investigation officer` FALSE EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `fine for` `s 82(3) — contravening the regulations` FALSE EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `months for` `s 82(3) — contravening the regulations` FALSE EQUALS 6

§§ `Goal 8c — composition, officers, the Government (ss 72, 73, 76, 77)`

-- s 76(1): the lower of half the maximum fine and $5,000
